# Four-ply info spelling from Stockfish sf_19 (edb0d9d), read 2026-11-24:
# UCIEngine::on_update_full in src/uci.cpp and SearchManager::output_pv in src/search.cpp.
# fisher-r6y D41 and fisher-8hc.6 stage this spelling, awaiting the owner's
# approval at merge. D3-D6 supply the
# existing principal variation and allowances, with time at least one under D41.
# The fisher-2aj.2 sources below supply the retained scores, node counts and response order.
# Sources: April 2006 UCI specification https://backscattering.de/chess/uci/
# and the owner decision of 2026-11-23 to reject opposite check with one
# diagnostic. Shakmaty 0.30.3 independently rejects the second FEN.
# Search: fisher-2aj rules 1 to 7 and 10. Exact search values
# were checked by exhaustive enumeration with python-chess 1.11.2.
# Searched transcript written 2026-11-23.
> position fen 7k/8/5K1Q/8/8/8/8/8 b - - 0 1
# White to move while the black king on e8 is attacked by the rook on e1.
> position fen 4k3/8/8/8/8/8/8/4RK2 w - - 0 1
# Owner decision of 2026-11-23: one diagnostic naming the check.
< info string {message:in check}
> isready
# UCI isready/readyok.
< readyok
> go
# Rules 4, 5, 7 and 10. Black must play h8g8, then h6g7 is checkmate.
# Python-chess counts 1, 21, 30 and 730 nodes at plies 1 to 4.
< info depth 4 multipv 1 score mate -1 nodes 782 nps {nps} time {time} pv {pv}
# Owner-approved example: the original position still has its sole legal move.
< bestmove h8g8
# UCI quit.
> quit
! exit
